  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1031 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nTuesday and Wednesday will be a couple of degrees warmer with dry\nconditions through the daylight hours of Wednesday. Models\ncontinue to agree on some medium PoPs Wednesday night into\nThursday as a shortwave diving out of the upper plains attempts to\nphase with another lobe of energy moving into the Great Lakes. \nThis will result in a large upper low rotating around a large \nportion of the eastern third of CONUS. Another lobe of energy will\nclip the area late Thursday which will result in some low PoPs on\nthe plateau. In addition to rain chances, some cooler air will be\ndrug southward with this system. We'll be back in the 30s \nThursday night and locations along the plateau will likely only \nmake it to the 40s on Friday. That cold air will stick around to \nstart next weekend with some 20s likely showing up Saturday\nmorning.",
